                <pb facs="1197" n="1705" xml:id="pg1705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Forrestal Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Diary Entry for December 31, 1948, by the Secretary of
                        Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forrestal</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-12-31">December 31, 1948</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Cabinet—China—Palestine</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Subject this morning at Cabinet was China.</p>
                <p>[Here follow two paragraphs concerning China.]</p>
                <p>Palestine:</p>
                <p>Lovett said the Israeli troops had apparently invaded Egypt. Specifically, they
                    were reported to have attacked an air field within the Egyptian border; that it
                    was reported the British would notify us that the failure of the Israelis to
                    withdraw promptly would automatically bring into operation the Anglo-Egyptian
                    mutual defense pact.</p>
            </div>
